<p>Our design system uses a comprehensive color token system that automatically adapts to light and dark themes. All colors are defined as CSS variables, making theme switching seamless and efficient.</p>
<h2 class="bold" id="design-token-philosophy"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="color-palette#design-token-philosophy">Design Token Philosophy</a></h2>
<p>Every color in our system is defined as a <strong>semantic token</strong> rather than a literal color value. This means colors have meaningful names like <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">text-default</span></span></code></span> and <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">surface-primary</span></span></code></span> instead of <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">black</span></span></code></span> or <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">white</span></span></code></span>. This approach enables:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Theme flexibility</strong>: Colors automatically adapt to light/dark modes</li>
<li><strong>Semantic clarity</strong>: Color names describe their purpose, not their appearance</li>
<li><strong>Maintainability</strong>: Centralized color definitions that can be updated globally</li>
<li><strong>Consistency</strong>: Guaranteed color harmony across all components</li>
</ul>
