<h2 class="bold" id="migration-from-legacy-colors"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="color-palette#migration-from-legacy-colors">Migration from Legacy Colors</a></h2>
<p>If you&#x27;re migrating from the legacy color system, see our <a href="../utilities/color#migration-guide" class="underline">Color Utilities - Migration Guide</a> for complete mapping between old and new class names.</p>
<h2 class="bold" id="best-practices"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="color-palette#best-practices">Best Practices</a></h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Use semantic names</strong>: Choose color classes based on their purpose, not appearance</li>
<li><strong>Theme-first mindset</strong>: Always consider how your design works in both light and dark themes</li>
<li><strong>Test both themes</strong>: Verify your components look good in both <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">.is-light</span></span></code></span> and <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">.is-dark</span></span></code></span> modes</li>
<li><strong>Leverage inheritance</strong>: Apply theme classes at the highest appropriate level</li>
<li><strong>Use CSS variables</strong>: Reference <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">var(--color-*)</span></span></code></span> variables in custom CSS for theme consistency</li>
<li><strong>Override sparingly</strong>: Only override theme at component level when truly necessary</li>
<li><strong>Maintain contrast</strong>: Always verify text/background combinations meet accessibility standards</li>
</ol>
